    "कामी/विश्वकर्मा is an ethno-linguistic Indo-Aryan Nepali speaking group. It is a Khas occupational caste belonging to blacksmiths. The 1854 Nepalese Muluki Ain not keep in lowest category. Kami are categorized under \"Hill Dalit\" among the 9 broad social groups, along with Damai, Badi, Sarki and Gaine by the Government of Nepal. Thus, the tribal designation of Khas is given only in few context to Kami ",
    "They live in Nepal, Sikkim and Darjeeling District of West Bengal, India. Kamis are essentially blacksmiths Kami/Vishowkarma are Vishowkarmabramin.are scattered across almost all hilly districts of Nepal, districts of Sikkim, Darjeeling, and Assam; some have settled in other parts of India as well. They are also known as Vishwakarma or Bishwakarma."
